<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Boyington returns six weeks after his intake visit, where he chose behavioral treatment for alcohol use disorder and was referred for trauma-focused psychotherapy. He began prolonged exposure therapy with Dr. Lee in behavioral health in early July and has attended five weekly sessions; Dr. Lee&apos;s consultation report came this morning. He has also gone to his veteran recovery peer group most weeks. Before treatment he drank most days, usually seven to nine drinks. In the six weeks since intake he drank on about four days, usually five beers. After a run of nightmares in the third week of therapy, when the imaginal exposure work began, he had one day of more than six drinks. He did not drive and called a peer from his group the next morning. He has had no tremor, sweats, or withdrawal symptoms. He sleeps about five and a half hours, with nightmares about twice a week instead of most nights, and he startles less at loud noises. He has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm since intake and still keeps the written safety plan in his wallet. He has lost 1.3 kg and attributes it to fewer drinks. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Drinking since intake</td><td>About four drinking days in six weeks, usually five beers; one day of more than six drinks after a run of nightmares; AUDIT-C 5, down from 10</td></tr><tr><td>Trauma symptoms</td><td>Nightmares about twice a week, down from most nights; less startle; PCL-5 31, down from 39</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Somewhat better; PHQ-9 6, down from 9, with item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Treatment engagement</td><td>Five prolonged exposure sessions with Dr. Lee; recovery peer group most weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, or plan since intake; safety plan kept and reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None, including no over-the-counter sleep aids</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

